# FinZee Architecture Rules

FinZee is a 100% offline, privacy-first Flutter personal finance app. There is no server, login, analytics, ads, or network sync.

## Rule 1 — Check dependencies before implementing a feature

Salary planning, savings, investments, bills, loans, and goals communicate through shared domain entities. Never implement a module that assumes another optional module is always on.

## Rule 2 — One source of financial truth

Never duplicate the same financial event. One transaction (or allocation completion that creates a transaction) must propagate to account balance, goals, dashboard, reports, and audit history.

## Rule 3 — OFF does not mean DELETE

Disabling a feature hides UI and stops automation. Database records stay. Historical reports stay valid. Re-enabling restores everything.

## Rule 4 — No business logic in widgets

UI → application service → domain logic → repository → Drift/SQLite.

## Rule 5 — Every database change needs a migration

Never change tables without a Drift migration.

## Rule 6 — Tests for every major feature

Unit tests for calculations/planning. Integration tests for Salary → Plan → Allocation → Transaction → Goal → Dashboard → Report.

## Rule 7 — Confirm destructive operations

Deletes, restore-overwrite, and feature-related data wipes require confirmation. Feature toggle OFF is not a wipe.

## Rule 8 — Versioned backups

JSON backup format is versioned (`finance_backup_v1`). Validate schema before restore. Create a safety backup before overwrite.

## Rule 9 — No silent regressions

Transfers are not expenses. Salary must not double-count. Savings/investments must not inflate income. Salary is never mandatory (Mode A works without it).

## Rule 10 — Update integrations when a module changes

Before completing a task, inspect affected modules (planning engine, calculations, reports, dashboard, backup).

## Privacy

No registration, login, email, cloud, backend, analytics SDK, ads, bank APIs, or network sync.
